{"name":"Icy Plains","hex":"#cfdafb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"icy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to, resembling, or abounding in ice; cold; frosty.","Covered with ice, wholly or partially."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/icy"},{"term":"plains","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of plain"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of plain"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plains"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plain","blocks":[{"text":"In geography, a plain, commonly known as flatland, is a flat expanse of land that generally has few rapid or steep changes in elevation. Natural vegetation in plains can include prairies/grasslands, forests, savanah, tundra, and desert biomes, among others. Plains occur as lowlands along valleys or at the base of mountains, as coastal plains, and as plateaus or uplands. Plains are one of the major landforms on earth, being present on all continents and covering more than one-third of the world's land area. Plains in many areas are important for agriculture. There are various types of plains, and biomes on them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Maniototoevening.jpg/330px-Maniototoevening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain","wikidata":"Q160091"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Horton_Plains_2021.jpg/500px-Horton_Plains_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Horton_Plains_2021.jpg/1280px-Horton_Plains_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Horton_Plains_2021.jpg/500px-Horton_Plains_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp